{number: 148}
{title: Yesterday, Today, Forever}
{key: C}

{start_of_verse: 1}
Oh, [C] how sweet the glorious message
Simple [F] faith may [C] claim;
Yesterday, today, forever,
[G7] Jesus is the [C] same!
Still He loves to save the sinful,
Heal the [F] sick and [C] lame,
Cheer the mourner, still the tempest.
[G7] Glory to His [C] name!
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
[C] Yesterday, today, forever,
[F] Jesus is the [C] same.
All may change, but Jesus never!
Glory to His [G7] name!
[C] Glory to His [F] name!
[C] Glory to His [G7] name!
All may change, but Jesus [C] never!
Glory to His [G7] [C] name!
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: 2}
Him [C] who pardon'd erring Peter,
Never [F] need'st thou [C] fear;
He that came to faithless Thomas,
[G7] All thy doubt will [C] clear.
He who let the lov'd disciple
On His [F] bosom [C] rest
Bids thee still, with love as tender,
[G7] Lean upon His [C] breast.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 3}
He [C] who mid the raging billows
Walk'd up-[F] on the [C] sea
Still can hush our wildest tempest,
[G7] As on Gali-[C] lee
He who wept and pray'd in anguish,
In Geth-[F] sema-[C] ne,
Drinks with us each cup of trembling,
[G7] In our ago-[C] ny.
{end_of_verse}
